The local PR workspace at the reviewed `headSha` is the only code a finding may cite. Before publish, `assertFindingsHaveEvidence` (`src/review/findings/evidenceValidator.ts`) keeps a finding only when the work-item `EvidenceLedger` `covers` its path and line range at that `headSha`; others are rejected as `no_evidence` or, for paths outside a `sparse` `CheckoutCoverage`, `sparse_path_no_evidence`. The ledger (`src/review/findings/evidenceLedger.ts`) is fed by `recordDeliveredFileRead` in `src/review/findings/evidenceLedger.ts` from the delivered result of `tools.read_pinned` (minus `clampedLines`, prefix or byte-budget cuts) and `tools.getWorkspaceDiff` (right-side ranges), never from the raw tool read. `searchWorkspace`, `findFiles`, and `resolveSymbol` record nothing, so their hits locate code but cannot back a citation; read the range first. A result with `truncation` set or a refused path cannot prove a symbol is absent. Guard: `test/evidenceValidator.test.ts`.
